---
description: Frontend uses generated OpenAPI types; no TS backend
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript frontend

Do

- Use generated types from the backend OpenAPI for request/response shapes.
- Keep UI state in the frontend; keep model/TTS work on the Python API.
- Cover empty, loading, and error states with real copy.

Don’t

- Define a parallel TypeScript backend or duplicate API models by hand.
- Hard-code secrets or remote LLM endpoints.
